// North-row lot (housing frame, top-middle slot) — same dir="up"
// orientation as the Mansion: native y=0 is the far-from-road content,
// native y=HEIGHT is nearest the road.
//
// Source photo showed a two-house repeat with no clean per-lot seam (the
// garage/driveway sit off-center within each repeat, bleeding across any
// simple half-width split) — extracted one full, uncut copy first (both
// border tree rows, full garage, full gate), then trimmed for the same
// reason as the Mansion: too tall to fit above the road without clipping
// the house.
//
// Three passes before this one got the fence wrong. First dropped it
// mid-structure, through its own flower-bed base. Second kept the whole
// fence/hedge/flower-bed assembly and just scaled it down ~25%, but that
// band is inherently a much denser design in this photo than the
// Mansion's own fence (a sparse iron line with open lawn around it, not
// a stacked fence+hedge+flower-bed border) — scaling the same content
// down still left it reading far heavier right at the sidewalk than its
// neighbor. This version instead keeps only the iron fence itself (its
// own rail is a clean, complete-looking edge on its own — no hedge, no
// flower bed), and pads the rest of the depth with a flat lawn-green
// fill instead of real photo content, so what actually sits near the
// sidewalk is sparse fence-then-open-lawn, matching the Mansion's own
// proportions instead of a dense garden border.
export const SUBURBAN_HOUSE_LOT_GROUND_STRIP_TOP = 0;
export const SUBURBAN_HOUSE_LOT_GROUND_STRIP_HEIGHT = 1;
